# DIBAY Support FAB Visibility HARD LOCK

Full spec: `docs/support-center/support-fab-visibility-owner-lock.md`.

## DO

- Enable Support FAB only via `SupportContextProvider` / `OwnerSupportContextBridge` with `enabled: true`.
- Use `openSupportCenter(context)` as the single entry from FAB and inline CTAs.
- Register new candidate routes in `lib/support/support-fab-route-registry.ts`.
- Run `npm run verify:support-fab-visibility-contract` when touching support FAB wiring.

## DO NOT

- Mount a global Support FAB without per-screen `enabled` context.
- Add `resolveSupportContextFromPathname()` or URL-prefix tables for FAB visibility.
- Infer FAB visibility from user role or pathname in `SupportFabHost`.
- Open `/mypage/inquiries` directly from `SupportFab` (use `openSupportCenter`).

## Global mount

`SupportFabHost` lives in `ConditionalAppShell` and reads the FAB registry only. Page providers publish context on mount and reset to `DISABLED_SUPPORT_CONTEXT` on unmount.
